# Pre-Demo Workflow

When preparing a Factorial demo for a client:

## 1. Read inputs

- `cliente.config.json` — clientName, clientSlug, language, industry, demoGoal, focusModules
- `transcricao/reuniao.txt` — research notes, SDR notes, LinkedIn, company website, or call transcript
- `demo/TEMPLATE-pre-demo.md` — structure for output
- `demo/areas-discovery.md` — discovery question bank

## 2. Research client

Summarize what you learned about the client (operations, scale, pain points). Do not invent facts not in the notes.

## 3. Map pains to Factorial (documentation only)

For each likely pain area, search official Factorial documentation (see factorial-documentation-assistant rule). Only recommend modules and features confirmed in help center or API docs. Cite URLs.

## 4. Generate client prep file

Create or update `demo/clientes/{clientSlug}/prep.md` from `demo/TEMPLATE-pre-demo.md` with:

- Client-specific context in sections 1–2
- Relevant discovery areas emphasized in section 3
- Focus modules for section 6 (demo) aligned with `focusModules` in config
- Closing script adapted to client language and industry

## 5. Update web demo guide

Update `src/data/demoGuideSteps.ts` and `src/utils/constants.ts`:

- Replace placeholders with client name, industry, demo goal
- Customize section 2 (What We Learned) from research notes
- Set discovery checklist items from prep
- Link demo videos from `src/data/factorialDemoVideos.ts` for focus modules

## 6. Do not

- Generate commercial proposals or pricing slides (out of scope)
- Use `docs/factorial-funcionalidades-modulos.md` for product feature names in the demo guide
- Invent client facts or Factorial capabilities
